// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-panics.py %S/Inputs/oom --real
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-opt-matrix.py --gopp %gopp --root %S --link-flags "%gopp_link_flags" --jobs 2 oom/
// P04.13 (docs/design/pipelines.md section 1): an allocation that fails ends
// the program with "fatal error: runtime: out of memory" and exit status 2
// at every `opt` level. LLVM's optimizer knows malloc, calloc and realloc and
// would delete an allocation whose memory does not escape, with the
// runtime's check, above opt 0 (review R6); the code generator declares them
// `nobuiltin` (codegen/alloc-nobuiltin.test has the IR). Real binaries: the
// fast runner's executor may be built with a sanitizer, whose calloc aborts
// instead of returning null. Go prints its own words for it ("runtime: out
// of memory: cannot allocate ..."), so Inputs/oom/*.out and .err are written
// by hand.
